# Curvature programme

Read `experiments/curvature_program/AGENT_CONTEXT.md` before changing geometry code or proposing a run.

- Treat every existing `outputs/` tree as immutable. New work gets a new output path.
- Inspect frozen `COMPLETE.json` / `decision.json` / tables; do not reuse remembered numbers.
- Do not train autoencoders, refit Q charts, or rerun permutations/bootstraps unless explicitly authorized.
- Keep signed split-half estimates; do not clamp; do not average-then-square.
- Name the estimator (D-full, D-residual, Q `KHcross`, `Kdircross`, task-aligned, mismatch). Do not write a generic `curvature()`.
- Preserve `sample_id` joins. Use leakage-safe \(w\) and train-only \(H_y\).
- Stop when a reliability gate fails. The Hessian-mismatch label is `label_hessian_unreliable`.
- Never edit a manuscript automatically. Never modify `src/effdim/` for this work.
